    title: "FindBaseNumber() — is it a factorial?",
    source: "9618/22 Winter 2022 Q6(a)",
    marks: 7,
    difficulty: 2,
    chapter: "Ch11 Programming",
    requirement: "FUNCTION FindBaseNumber(ThisValue : INTEGER) RETURNS INTEGER",
    prompt: [
      "The factorial of an integer n is n × (n−1) × ... × 2 × 1, for example the factorial",
      "of 5 is 120.",
      "",
      "A function `FindBaseNumber()` is called with a positive, non-zero integer. It",
      "returns the `BaseNumber` if the parameter value is the factorial of that number,",
      "and returns −1 if the parameter value is not a factorial.",
      "",
      "For example, 120 returns 5, 6 returns 3 and 12 returns −1.",
      "",
      "Write pseudocode for `FindBaseNumber()`."
    ].join("\n"),
    model: `FUNCTION FindBaseNumber(ThisValue : INTEGER) RETURNS INTEGER
    DECLARE Num : INTEGER
    DECLARE Try : INTEGER
    Try <- 1
    FOR Num <- 1 TO ThisValue
        Try <- Try * Num
        IF Try = ThisValue THEN
            RETURN Num
        ENDIF
    NEXT Num
    RETURN -1
ENDFUNCTION`,
